Implement US-01 frontend tasks T008, T009, T011 from `specs/002-us-01-policyholder-vehicle-form/tasks.md` (read spec.md, plan.md, research.md R8–R10, data-model.md, contracts/form-fields-api.md; load the `angular-conventions` skill). Do NOT commit. Other agents work in parallel: do NOT touch `frontend/src/app/features/quote-form/validation/**` (owned by another agent), `shared/ui/**`, `styles.scss`, or routes.

Shared type contract (another agent creates `frontend/src/app/features/quote-form/validation/validation.model.ts` with exactly this; import from it, do not create it):
```ts
export type FieldType = 'text' | 'number' | 'select' | 'date' | 'checkbox';
export interface NamedRule { name: string; value: number | null; }
export interface FieldRules { type: FieldType; required: boolean; min: number | null; max: number | null; pattern: string | null; validators: NamedRule[]; }
export type FieldValue = string | boolean;
```

- T008: `core/country`: add `legalAge: number | null` to `CountryDto`, `legalAge: number` to `Country` (mapper: missing/null/negative → 18), `fields[2]=legalAge` in `CountryService` params. Update existing mapper tests + add `describe('US-01 · FR-007 country legal age', ...)`. Fix any existing tests/fixtures constructing Country objects.
- T009: `features/quote-form/data/`: `form-field.model.ts` with Strapi DTOs per the contract (FormFieldDto, FormValidationsDto, FormValidatorDto, FormOptionDto, FormFieldsResponseDto) and app models:
```ts
export type FormSection = 'policyholder' | 'vehicle';
export interface FieldOption { label: string; value: string; }
export interface FormFieldDescriptor { key: string; label: string; type: FieldType; required: boolean; helpText: string | null; placeholder: string | null; errorMessage: string; order: number; section: FormSection; options: FieldOption[]; rules: FieldRules; }
export interface FormSections { policyholder: FormFieldDescriptor[]; vehicle: FormFieldDescriptor[]; }
```
`form-field.mapper.ts`: pure `mapFormFields(dtos): FormSections` — group by section, sort by order (stable), drop unknown types and unknown sections with console.warn, null validations → empty rules, null options → [], rules.required mirrors required. `form-field.service.ts`: `FormFieldService.load(countryCode: string): Observable<FormSections>` calling relative `/api/form-fields` with the exact contract query (country code UPPER case in the filter, sort, populate, pageSize 100); no caching needed beyond a simple per-call request. Unit tests `describe('US-01 · FR-002 …')` etc. for the mapper.
- T011: `core/session/quote-session.store.ts`: data shape `{ step1?: Record<string, string | boolean>, step1Completed?: boolean }` stored in existing `data`. Add `readStep1(): Record<string, string|boolean>`, `saveStep1(values)` (writes and clears step1Completed), `markStep1Completed()`, `isStep1Completed(): boolean`. `hasData()` = true only if some step1 value is a non-empty string (trimmed) or `true`. Keep `start`/`discardData`/`clear` behaviour (discarding clears step1 and completed). Tolerant to corrupt data. Unit tests `describe('US-01 · FR-009 …')` including: save/restore, hasData false for all-empty, step1Completed cleared by save, discard. Keep existing US-00 tests passing (update ones whose assumptions about hasData change, explaining why).

Verify with `npm --prefix frontend run verify` — note the validation.model.ts may not exist yet when you start; if so, create NOTHING there; instead wait/retry verify at the end, and if it still does not exist report that type errors are only the missing import. Report files changed and test results.

